{
  "dom_id": "step-e9692",
  "name": "Example: Using Trend Line Equations to Make a Prediction",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/ecce4e60594a69e040328cc8f65300f7ad1ecfe20806d9be08f154fe2beb1246.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between a book\u2019s spine thickness (in millimetres) and the total number of pages for a random sample of children's books. The equation of the trend line is $y = 10x.$ Assuming this trend continues, estimate the thickness of a book with $200$ pages.",
  "worked_solution": "To predict the thickness in a book with $200$ pages, we need to substitute $y = 200$ into the equation of the trend line and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =10x \\\\ 200 & =10x \\\\ \\frac{200}{10} & =x \\\\ 20 & =x \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, according to this model, a book with $200$ pages should have approximately a thickness of $20\\text{ mm}.$\n\n**Note:** The point where $y=200$ is not shown on our trend line. Therefore, our result *may* be unreliable.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-e9692\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n                 \n                <div class=\"example\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Example:</span> Using Trend Line Equations to Make a Prediction</div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"e9692\">?</div>\n                    </div>\n            \n                    <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                        <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                 